From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wineboot: do not start a Startup folder's desktop.ini

Purpose: a prefix update (wineboot -u) no longer opens the Startup folder's
desktop.ini in Notepad and keeps the prefix busy.
Windows behavior: the Startup folder of Windows 7 (and XP) holds a
desktop.ini for its localized name, hidden and system; Windows does not
start it at logon. Protected system files (hidden and system) are not
listed unless asked for (SHCONTF_INCLUDESUPERHIDDEN).
Wine before: ProcessStartupItems enumerates the folder with
SHCONTF_INCLUDEHIDDEN, which in Wine's shell32 lists hidden system files
too, and ShellExecute opened desktop.ini in Notepad. The Notepad kept the
prefix's server running, so waiting for it (wineserver -w) after an update
timed out.
Change: items that are both hidden and system are skipped.
Evidence: with the Windows 7 shell prefix's Startup desktop.ini (attributes
0x6), wineboot -u started NOTEPAD.EXE ...\StartUp\desktop.ini; with the
change it starts nothing there.
Scope: everywhere; other startup items (hidden or not) start as before.
---
 programs/wineboot/wineboot.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
index 1e2a7b7..3fb13f4 100644
--- a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
+++ b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
@@ -1750,6 +1750,13 @@ static BOOL ProcessStartupItems(void)
 	    hr = StrRetToBufW(&strret, pidlItem, wszCommand, MAX_PATH);
 	    if (FAILED(hr))
 		WINE_TRACE("Unable to parse display name.\n");
+	    else if ((GetFileAttributesW(wszCommand) & (FILE_ATTRIBUTE_HIDDEN | FILE_ATTRIBUTE_SYSTEM)) ==
+                     (FILE_ATTRIBUTE_HIDDEN | FILE_ATTRIBUTE_SYSTEM) &&
+                     GetFileAttributesW(wszCommand) != INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES)
+            {
+                /* protected system files (the folder's desktop.ini) are not startup items */
+                WINE_TRACE("Skipping %s.\n", wine_dbgstr_w(wszCommand));
+            }
 	    else
             {
                 HINSTANCE hinst;
